-- title:
--   Weight p+1 level N to weight 2 level Np
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $N\ge 1$ with $p\nmid N$, and assume that if $p=3$ then $N$ has a prime divisor $q$ with $q\equiv 2\pmod 3$. Let $S$ be a set of natural numbers with $p\notin S$, let $F$ be a field of characteristic $p$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from `heckeAlgebra N ((p : ℤ) + 1) S` to $F$, that is, from the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\,S_{p+1}(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$ (so including $T_p$) together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q\mid N$ with $q\notin S$. Then, with $S'=S\cup\{q : q \text{ prime},\ q\mid N\}$, there exists a ring homomorphism $\theta_2$ from `heckeAlgebra (N * p) 2 S'`, the corresponding subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}\,S_2(\Gamma_0(Np))$, to $F$ such that: for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\nmid Np$, $\ell\notin S$ and $\ell\notin S'$ one has $\theta_2(T_\ell)=\theta(T_\ell)$; and $\theta_2(U_p)=\theta(T_p)$, the divisibility $p\mid Np$ and the non-membership $p\notin S'$ being passed as arguments to the generators.
--
--   This is the classical trade of weight for level for mod $p$ Hecke eigensystems on $\Gamma_0$: an eigensystem of weight $p+1$ and level $N$ prime to $p$ is realised in weight $2$ and level $Np$, with the $T_p$-eigenvalue becoming the $U_p$-eigenvalue; the present version carries the side condition at $p=3$ requiring a prime factor of $N$ congruent to $2$ modulo $3$. It feeds the construction of a stable line for the associated Galois representation in [`GaloisRep.exists_stableLine_of_theta_T_ne_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_three_le_of_eq_three`](thm.html#GaloisRep.exists_stableLine_of_theta_T_ne_zero_of_det_eq_pow_of_three_le_of_eq_three).
